On 2 Jan 2002, Barry Roberts wrote:
> I am running tomcat on a Digital Server 5000 with RedHat 7.1.  I need
> to get JDBC to Oracle 8 working.  Is that possible?  I can't find an
> Oracle client for Alpha Linux.
> 
> Is the Thin JDBC driver my only option?  I think I have that working.

That's your only option, unless you can coax the Digital Unix client into
working.  (But note that the DU JDK has no chance of running on
Alpha/Linux, so the type-2 driver is probably a no-go.)

The thin driver works fine, as long as you don't need BLOBs.  I use it all
the time.

Jeff




