> smoothly, but it works.  Unfortunately, the patch is quite lengthy,
> so I can't append it here. There is no need for assembler code,
> except for speed.

I'm currently working on optimizing the ffmpeg divx engine, which is
is for example used in mplayer, for Alpha/MVI (I think a PC164 has
MVI, too?). Perhaps you're interested in exchanging patches? The main
time sink is currently the IDCT; unfortunately, I have no idea how to
speed it up further...

        Falk




