>
> Sun doesn't build StarOffice for Alpha Linux, but you could try 
> building OpenOffice from source.  Have a look at
> http://www.openoffice.org/ if you want to try this route.

I tried to build OO (build 638, IIRC) on Alpha RH7.1, and it
didn't even get halfway to first base.  (The build tools are
_very_ complex and convoluted!)

Applix 4.4.1 (now 4.4.2) used to be able to read most M$Worst
and some PPT files, but it quit working for me.  Other people
with Alpha Linux have seen the same problem, but I haven't
found a solution, at least not for my system.

The Linux Journal had an article in the November issue, issue
number 91, on word processors and translators for Linux.  Many
are available in source form.  I installed a couple of them,
but I haven't been able to test them on actual .doc files.
You might check LJ's web site for the list of URLs.  Please
inform if you need them, and I'll type them in and email them.

Good luck.

