Just a quick note on the new kernel and an old PC164 with 2.4.17: 

1. Works great, compiles out of the box. 

*note*
I changed to "generic" kernel because specifying PC164 causes the GCC 
compiler options to specify MARCH=EV6 which the straight PC164's were not. 

Boots well and the "machine locks up under ethernet load" bugaboo seems to 
be gone.  Couple of performance tests (http load and CGI load) shows that 
the machine is more than 30% faster performing these tests than the stock RH 
7.1 install. 

I'm still testing at the moment, but I thought I'd report preliminary good 
news to the list.  Previously my CGI test program would cause the stock 
kernel to start to swap at a very low load and the machine would start to 
crawl. 

PS (is RH 7.2 going to come or no? Just curious.) 

Speedracer 


