On Mon, Jan 07, 2002 at 07:20:37PM +0000, Speedracer wrote:
> 
> *note*
> I changed to "generic" kernel because specifying PC164 causes the GCC 
> compiler options to specify MARCH=EV6 which the straight PC164's were not. 

Huh?

Just tried building 2.4.17 for PC164 under RH 7.0 (GCC 2.96-85), and
saw it issuing only:

	-Wa,-mev6

which is NOT the same thing as -mcpu=ev6; -Wa,-mev6 just tells the
assembler to allow EV6 instructions to be assembled, if it encounters
them in its input.

However, I did NOT see any -mcpu=xxx issued, which is bad, since PC164
is EV56 and could use the byte/word instructions. Here's a little patch
to make this happen - see if it helps in any way, or at least make sure
it doesn't hurt anything... ;-}

diff -ur LINUX/linux-2.4.17/arch/alpha/Makefile PATCH/linux-2.4.17/arch/alpha/Makefile
--- LINUX/linux-2.4.17/arch/alpha/Makefile      Sun Dec  3 20:45:20 2000
+++ PATCH/linux-2.4.17/arch/alpha/Makefile      Tue Jan  8 10:41:38 2002
@@ -56,6 +56,14 @@
     CFLAGS := $(CFLAGS) -mcpu=ev4
     mcpu_done := y
   endif
+  ifeq ($(mcpu_done)$(CONFIG_ALPHA_PC164),ny)
+    CFLAGS := $(CFLAGS) -mcpu=ev56
+    mcpu_done := y
+  endif
+  ifeq ($(mcpu_done)$(CONFIG_ALPHA_EV5),ny)
+    CFLAGS := $(CFLAGS) -mcpu=ev5
+    mcpu_done := y
+  endif
   ifeq ($(mcpu_done)$(CONFIG_ALPHA_EV67)$(have_mcpu_ev67),nyy)
     CFLAGS := $(CFLAGS) -mcpu=ev67
     mcpu_done := y

> PS (is RH 7.2 going to come or no? Just curious.) 

Yes, it is.

--Jay++

