On Mon, Jan 07, 2002 at 11:26:15AM -0600, Aaron wrote:
>
> I pray the Qlogic ISP driver in the upcoming Redhat 7.2 AXP is working.  I
> was never able to load Redhat 7.1 on my Digital Server 3300 because of this
> issue.

AFAICT, the stock qlogicisp.c driver used in RH 7.1, and the one in
some pre-beta RH 7.2 kernel sources I've seen, are nearly identical,
thus I don't think the problem has (yet) gone away. The problem seems
to be most common on machines/cards with the older 1020 chipset, and
with a single SCSI chain that includes both HDD and CD, even with a
reasonable active terminator. And you can (usually) forget about
attaching magtape or CD-RW regardless of the QLogic chipset, as the
stock driver is *very* poor with those.

HOWEVER, there is another QLogic driver that appears much better
maintained and does work (for me :-) in the problematic cases I've
looked into, namely AS500 (ALCOR/XLT) and AS800 (NORITAKE), both with
a builtin QLogic 1020 on the motherboards. Info/downloads can be found
at:

	http://www.feral.com/isp.html		# (Hi, Matt! :-)

with patch sets that apply against a number of the 2.4.x kernels.

To test the new driver out, I patched the new driver into the stock
RH 7.1 kernel sources (2.4.3-12), and subsequently built a bootable
floppy image containing the binary. Using the standard floppy-install
scenario on both AS500 and AS800, I sucessfully installed the entire 2
CD RH 7.1 distro, which I'd not been able to do with the released
CDs. This floppy image can be found for anonFTP on gatekeeper.dec.com:

	/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/rh71boot.img

If you're willing, give it a try and let me know what happens.

Also, if you use that new driver for other purposes, ie to try to
solve XP1000 problems, it would also be worth knowing how it worked.

Good luck!

--Jay++

