Hi everyone;

I'm trying to install RH 7.1 on my XL-366 workstation and cannot get MILO to
boot properly when using the xlt.img disk as found on the RH7.1 installer
CD.  It gets to the point where it is swapping the PAL code and it hangs.

I've found a 5 year old MILO disk built against the 2.0 kernel, and it boots
properly to the Milo prompt, but when I try to boot the kernel on the
generic.img (from RH7.1cd) disk it hangs there.  My feelings are that that
build of MILO doesn't support the new kernel on the boot disk.

Any suggestions?  I just don't know what to do from here--I feel like the
xlt.img disk on the RH cd should work and can't figure out why it hangs.
Anyone else with an XL366 able to get this disk to work?

Thanks for the help

-ger




