I don't remember which SRM I have and my machine is busy doing some 
important data sorting and formating and I don't expect it to be done for at 
least a day or so. Try this, if the SRM you have doesn't see your HD 
controller, go out and get a cheap IDE drive and throw it in for you boot 
partition.  That way you would boot off from the IDE drive, but everything 
else would be scsi and only /boot would actually be on IDE. 

I hope this helps, when the machine is done doing what it needs to do I'll 
take it down and see which SRM is installed. 

Aaron 

