Mark Arrasmith wrote:

> Do I have understand this right . . .
>
> The upcoming 7.2 release is only for 264 cpus and not the older boxes?
>
> Also, is it possible to create install disks from the rawhide tree?  I've
> been happy running Redhat on my 164 and 064 based workstations and servers
> for awhile.  And I'm not really looking forward to mixing up Debian and
> RedHat distributions to support.

Well, I'd expect pca56 ev56 would work which I think pulls in the majority of
the
XX164 and above models. the 21064 based machines.. erm.... thats what ebay
is for. right? <runs away>

No the practicallity is that there are two C libs one that does NOT have ev6
instructions
and one that does. That takes up space on the distribution media. Similarly,
we would have to build specific kernels for ev5 ev56 ev6 ev67 ev68 in BOOT,
uniprocessor and  multiprocessor forms. This again would eat up a lot of
distribution media space and make the installation proceedure very difficult
to
automate correctly.

This said, there is NOTHING to stop you from rebuilding the SRPMS from
rawhide
or the eventual 7.2 tree with an older Clib that only uses ev4 instructions

Very simply we can't go and create specalized versions of all the packages
for each
architecture so a compromise has to be struck and the unfortunate consequence
is
that the older machines will effectively be shut out from the nice shiny CD
installion
media

I hope that explains

Phil
=--=




