> From: ken.siersma@ekkinc.com
> Date: Sun, 13 Jan 2002 11:08:24 -0500
>
> Why did you need to upgrade the server?  I have a very similar setup -
> RH 7.1 with UP2000 single processor - and I see a log of unaligned trap
> messages from X in my syslog.  I believe many of these errors eventually
> cause the machine to crash, because often I come in in the morning and
> find the alpha down, but the only thing I find in the messages is the
> unaligned trap errors caused by X.  I'm not currently running X, and the
> system has been up for over a week now.
>
> So, first, did you use the Comaq or gcc compilers to compile X, and do
> you see any unaligned trap messages in the system log?

With the standard RH7.1 setup, using a TNT2 Vanta graphics
card, my system has been stable.  I do see unaligned trap
messages, mostly from xlock.  On my system, I don't see any
evidence of anything that would cause a crash, with the
Vanta.

When I tried an Oxygen VX1 card, it didn't work, and it
appeared to cause a crash with XFree 4.0.3.  There were
strange artifacts on the screen, as if something were
scribbling on wrong places in the video RAM.

I am trying XFree 4.1.0 in order to try to restore some
functionality, 24-bit color at 1600x1200 resolution, that
worked just fine with a Voodoo3-3K (PCI) card with RH6.1
and has not worked even once since I moved from RH6.1 to
RH7*.  I used the default compilation and makefiles, which
I would think would be gcc rather than the Compaq compiler,
especially since I have not explicitly installed the
Compaq compiler.  I still see unaligned trap messages, but
(so far, so good) I don't see evidence of system instability.

My experience indicates the graphics card has a lot to do
with system stability issues.  For me, a Permedia 2 card
worked okay, but it is slow.  A Voodoo3-3K was questionable,
but that card developed a hardware problem, so Voodoo might
be okay.  A TNT2 Vanta card works well as long as I don't
try 24-bit color.  An Oxygen VX1 card does not work with
4.0.3, but I have yet to try it with 4.1.0.

Good luck with your system situation.  Have you tried
other graphics cards and/or XFree 3.3.6?

Robert Riches
richesr1@inetarena.com




