>                                                         http://www.yelof.com
What's to comment?
It was inevitable.
Alphas may progress, but without new chipsets for smaller machines, the end 
was in sight a long time ago.
The 21264 single through quad processor machines made now use the same 
chipsets we saw in 1997.

API did not have the funding or will to design new chipsets. Compaq was not 
willing to spend the money.
Now Samsung is using PC chipsets to deal with this, with some good results.
At least they ARE still doing something and making progress, slowly but surely.


