I found solutions to two problems I had been seeing and had
mentioned (or thought I had) on this list:

  Netscape calling xkill:

    The solution is to edit /usr/bin/netscape (a shell script)
    and comment out the xkill command.  It does not work to put a
    modified version of the script in /usr/local/bin, apparently
    because the script appears to find other members of its
    family based on its current location.

  xlock aborting with an FP exception (signal 8) in invert mode:

    Install the xlockmore RPM, unpack the tarball, apply the
    ...c++ and ...implicit patches from the source RPM, add
    the -mieee option to the CFLAGS and CXXFLAGS variables in all
    Makefiles that set those variables, recompile, and put the
    xlock/xlock binary in /usr/local/bin.  (I had to use the
    --without-dpms switch when running ./configure.)

These were on RH7.1.  YMMV.

Have fun.  :-)

