Hello Helge,

AFAIK at the moment the Xenons are quite similar to the P4's, since
the Xenons with extended cache are not yet available. So you might
test on a P4.

What the SPEC values are worth depends. I have made some
tests here with linear programming codes and our 750/8M and 833/4M
Alphas are roughly equivalent to the P4/1.7=20

BUT

- one thing is that the SPEC values for Intel are made with the Intel
  compiler which has some bias to generate wrong code in the highest=20
  optimization levels if you compile something else than the SPEC code.

- It depends very much on what you do. Have a look at MCF from=20
  SPECint. I know this code and in priciple it just measures
  random memory accesses. That's the same with many of these=20
  codes. They all have one major bottleneck. You habe to find
  the one that has the same then yours.

Just my two (euro) cents.

Thorsten


