 From recent press releases, choose your favorite stock market site for the 
rest : 

"Compaq's services business now comprises 24 percent of its revenue, at 
approximately $2 billion, showing 8 per cent sequential growth and 4 percent 
growth over the prior year period. Revenue from the Enterprise Computing 
segment was up 15 percent from the third quarter to $2.7 billion." 

2.7 billion out of 8.5 billion makes enterprise computing 30% or so of 
Compaq's revenue.  I wonder how much "alpha" business is in the "service 
business" and the "enterprise computing business". 

Going to the web site and selecting enterprise solutions I see that all the 
big, groovy, really nifty got to have with lots of buzzword things are alpha 
powered. 

Hmmm, and let me get this right, they just GAVE AWAY alpha chip development 
to Intel, and they want to MERGE with HP and basically throw a majority of 
their enterprise stuff out on it's ear? (See SEC filing for merger)  Ipaq 
and alpha along with service seems to be the ONLY thing that Compaq has any 
margin on. 


