At 15:48 18/01/2002 +0200, Ted Lufoma wrote:
>Iam running Digital UNIX v4.0D on Digital Professional Workstation a-series
>(PWS 500a).
>I intend to migrate to Linux RedHat. What version of RedHat can i install on
>this box.????. Has anybody done this before.??
>Please advise ASAP.

Ted,

You can definitely run Linux on it. Search the mailing list archives to see 
some of the issues (no significant problems).

I've run Red Hat 6.2, SuSE 6.3 and SuSE 7.1 on mine (plus FreeBSD 4.4).

Things that mess people up:

Video Card: look through the lists for recommended cards. The more generic 
the better (mine has a Matrox Millenium II).

SCSI Card: if your machine has an Adaptec card (doubtful if it's already 
running digitalUNIX), you won't be able to boot from the SCSI drive (using 
SRM). I booted from a floppy until I replaced my Adaptec with a Tekram SCSI 
card.

Those two points account for 75% of people's starting problems.

Good Luck!

