With regards to your message at 07:53 PM 1/18/02, Greg Lindahl. Where you 
stated:
> > >My manual says 128 max, install in pairs, for a maximum of 512 meg
> > >memory (that's 4 128s)
> >
> > That is what the manual, which was written a long time ago, says.
> > It is out of date..
> > 4 x 256MB works. We have built over 400 with that..
>
>According to Compaq, the manual said that because there's a capitance
>issue with using 4x256 MB. You want to violate the spec, it's your
>call, but it can be as reliable as overclocking.
>
>g


Right.
As we have not seen a problem with this, and as this identical chipset , as 
sold by Compaq and Digital before that, was supplied in AS533 and 600's, 
with 1GB from the factory, I find that a bit dubious.

At least several thousand of these are out there with 1GB, and it is not an 
issue that seems to come up ever, I feel quite safe in saying 1GB is fine.
For that matter on the Samsung 164UX boards they provided 6 slots and lots 
of people ran 1.5GB on these without problems as well..

As you seem fond of APIs technical prowess, let's refer to their FAQ on 
memory on the PC164LX:
http://www.api-networks.com/support/faq_164lx_memory.shtml

Here they made specific recommendations for memory parts, including 256MB 
modules.



With our best regards,

