Something to try immediately: disable hardware cursor via:

	Option	"SWCursor"

in the Device Section. VX1 is nasty WRT the amount of time it takes
to change the cursor shape, and sometimes this causes problems.

Two other suggestions:

1. use a much later kernel, say 2.4.16/17, than the stock one in RH7.1
2. download and build XFree86 4.2.0 which is just released, I believe.

4.2.0 has a lot more fixes in the VX1 code, including multi-head,
which has also been fixed for the ELSA Permedia 2's and Matrox
Millennium I's. both the latter two have the VGA-disable DIP switches,
which are not needed on VX1 (SRM console does some funky business in
SW).

I'm currently running a dual VX1 setup in a DS20, 4.2.0/xinerama/gnome,
with reasonable stability.

Of course, YMMV, but if it does, PLEASE LET ME KNOW!

Good luck.

--Jay++

