Is there any way to use an updated JRE with either Netscape or
Mozilla?

The system in question is a UP2000 running Redhat 7.1, with
Netscape 4.77-1 and/or Mozilla 0.8.1-5.  I have the 1.3.1 JDK
from Compaq.

I'm trying to use a real-time stock quote service (money.net)
that requires the latest JVM (they say to download it from
Microsloth).  With netscape, the quote service window stays gray.
With Mozilla, some hint windows come up, and Mozilla downloads
the JRE for X86 with Losedows (oops!) and then wonders why it
does not install.

Is there a way of using the Compaq JDK's runtime environment
with either Netscape or Mozilla?

In case there is a solution for Mozilla but not for Netscape,
is there a way to make Mozilla just a tiny bit faster?  It
takes several seconds just to close an ordinary window.  Also,
is there a way to get Mozilla to honor the user-level xmodmap
entries that put the CTRL key function in the proper place on
the keyboard?

Thanks.

Robert Riches
