Hello,
Have a UP2000 that I some time ago put RH 7.1 on, and after recompiling the
kernel, I remember having trouble getting it to boot with SRM (I don't
remember exactly what it was doing). Anyway, I ended up booting from
AlphaBIOS instead of SRM, and now I cannot get the machine to go directly
into SRM.  I've tried the 'set os_type Unix' command as in the HOWTO, but it
still ends up booting from AlphaBIOS.

The worst part about this is that I would like to upgrade my kernel - I'm
currently running 2.4.12.  I don't have many complaints, but I want to run
2.4.17.  After installing my new kernel, I've tried to change the image that
AlphaBIOS boots with to the 2.4.17 image, but it refuses to acknowledge that
the 2.4.17 kernel exists.  I even tried renaming the 2.4.17 image to the
exact same name as the 2.4.12 kernel that AlphaBIOS is supposedly booting,
but it still ends up running 2.4.12.

I think successfully booting to SRM instead of AlphaBIOS will fix this.

Any ideas?

Thanks
