Hello !
On Thu, Jan 24, 2002 at 12:48:11PM -0500, Ken Siersma wrote:
> On Thursday 24 January 2002 11:42, you wrote:
> > -> > End up in SRM.  But, I 'boot dka0 -file 1/vmlinuz-2.4.17 -flag 
> > 'root=/ -> > dev/sda4' and it still boots 2.4.12.
> >
> >
> > Do you have /boot in a diferent partition than / ??
> > If not you need to specify the whole path to SRM.
> >
> 
> Are you sure?  I do have /boot in a different partition than /, but if I give 
> aboot -file 1/boot/vmlinuz-2.4.17, SRM can't find the image file.  If I do a 
> cat /etc/aboot.conf, on the top I see:
> 	# aboot default configurations
> 	# NOTICE:  You have a /boot partition.  This means that
> 	#          all kernel paths are relative to /boot/

Since everything is relative to /boot, also aboot.conf. So you need to
edit /boot/etc/aboot.conf in your case. If you look at the man pages
(if you have a recent aboot.conf) note that it always says
etc/aboot.conf not /etc/aboot.conf. Maybe you can post your disk
layout (/dev/sda1 is mounted as /boot ?). 

Greetings

       Helge

-- 
