On Thu, Jan 24, 2002 at 01:50:37PM -0500, Ken Siersma wrote:
> I tried giving aboot the -file vmlinuz-2.4.17, but it still boots 2.4.12.

In that case you likely have multiple copies of 'aboot.conf' on
different partitions and you are picking up a boot line and a boot image
not from where you think but from some default location (possibly
configured with a help of 'abootconf').  Or even from a different
disk if you have multiple disks with boot blocks on them.

You can be more specific where to find your vmlinuz-2.4.17 by typing
something like 1/vmlinuz-2.4.17 (here this means first partition).
I _think_ that even '-file' in SRM will accept that but for sure you
can do that typing at 'aboot>' prompt (boot with '-fl i' to get there).
And specify explicitely your boot device to avoid misunderstandings.

Another possibility is that what you call vmlinuz-2.4.17 actually is
a 2.4.12 boot image.  These names are only for your convenience and
equally well you could name that file run_spot_run.

  Michal




