What version of RH are you running?
kernel version?
Xfree version? stock, binary RPM, or handbuilt?

Is DRI being loaded? Check you /etc/X11/XF86Config
If so, Try disabling DRI by commenting out the
DRI and GLX lines in the modules section and try again. 

The last time I had DRI working was with XF4.1 Linux 2.4.12
on my LX running RH 7.0. That was a voodoo 3, worked very well.
I've been meaning to pick up a radeon... 

Peter

