Well, I finally managed to get DRI working with the Radeon PCI
in my LX164.  Previously, direct rendering was always disabled,
no matter what I tried.  Installing XF4.2 fixed the problem.  Once
this was working,  I decided to try out a few OpenGL games.  First,
I tried Quakeforge.  this seems to run quite well, except that it is
always windowed.

Next, I thought  that I would give the recently released Quake2
souce a shot.  I downloaded Relnev's version and everything
compiled smoothly.  By default, the OpenGL renderers are disabled
in the Makefile, so I made some minor revisions and these compliled
cleanly as well.  Pleasently surprised, I fired up the game and low and
behold, Quake2 was running on my alpha in GL.  Overall the game
was quite smooth, but I noticed a big slowdown with the dynamic
light flashes.  Disabling dynamic lights made it very playable, but I
have no idea why is so slow with them enabled.  I'm going to try to
rebuild DRI with the compaq math libraries and see if this makes
any difference.  Anyone have any ideas?


-Eric




