I compiled and replaced 2.2.14-6.0 with 2.4.17 on my XL-366 and I've
found two oddities I hope someone can help with.
=20
1) if I "shutdown -h now",  it gets to "power down" and reboots, whereas
2.2.14-6.0 would halt the machine.
2) during boot I see "NFS lockd: lockdsvc Function not implemented" -
what should I be doing in regard to that?
=20
Now, before I go and wreck the thing by trying to install 7.1 ...
=20
Is there a "words of one syllable" guide to compiling the kernel on
Alpha?=20
    what options should one include as a "must have" for a normal build
(for an XL366),=20
