On Saturday 26 January 2002 19:11, you wrote:
> I got the kernel to compile and install, but 2.4.17 kernel panics right
> after 'freeing unused kernel memory', says something about bad
> paging..at an address.
>
> Do I need to change something in my makefile?
>
> Ted
Hi,
I had the same thing, then I discovered
a) That I put "Discontiguous Memory Support" on,
b) "NUMA Support (NEW)" was also on and
c) "RAM disk support" with "Initial RAM disk (initrd) support" turned on.
After I unchecked these, it went well. So, if this doesn't work, try it once 
only with the options you are REALLY sure about (and not like poor me who 
thought: "oh, this sounds cool. I want it, too...")

Greets

Ineiti




