> I have a PC164 (It works too well to junk it:-) that is running RedHat 7.1
> and the kernel from the kernel-2.4.3-12 rpm. Works fine, apparently.
> I would like to run the kernel from the 2.4.9-21 rpm, but when I boot
> it the system clock runs 4X too slow. That is, "sleep 3" takes 12 seconds.
>
> I'm running a time demon, and it's happy with the 2.4.3 kernel behavior.
> It never synchronizes with the 2.4.9 kernel, though.
>
> I'm trying to keep a "canonical RedHat" system because I'm lazy and I'm
> letting up2date manage things for me. I can go back to building my own
> kernels, if there are known problems with the RedHat builds.




