Hello !
On Sat, Jan 26, 2002 at 04:09:18PM -0700, Maurice Hilarius wrote:
> With regards to your message at 10:11 AM 1/26/02, Ted Goodridge, Jr. Where 
> you stated:
> 
> >How do I get SRM to boot another kernel that s in the /boot partition 
> >(/dev/sda1)?  I cant seem to get it to boot anything other than the 
> >install kernel.
> 
> 
> Normally add an entry in /etc/aboot.conf?

Best way to test alternative entries in your etc/aboot.conf (probably
in your case in /boot/etc/):

boot dxx -fl "i"
(where you replace dxx with your ordinary boot device, i.e. dka, dqa, ..)

then press "l" to list all entries and try the new one by number, i.e.
by pressing "1". 

Greetings

        Helge

