Actually the Telluride was an EB64+ ( or very similar) IIRC.  If it is
anything like my Aspen Alpine, It has the firmware stored in a UV EPROM, so
if you have ARC, you have ARC, and can not update to SRM.

I just copied MILO to the windowsNT "system" ( or was that "boot" )
partition, whatever the FAT partition is on your hard drive.
once in MILO, I use the command line:

boot  sdb2:boot/vmlinuz root=/dev/sdb2

of course, use your own hard drive designations...

HTH...
