Don't know if this disqualifies your suggestion, but the Milo
recommended by Aspen when I got it going (3 years ago)
was the eb164.  It's a 275 MHz cpu, fairly old and with no 
IDE capabilities (strictly SCSI)

As far as I know, it has no SRM capabilities - how would I check?

As you may be able to tell, I've been pretty much on my own
on this thing.

And w/o the capabilities to download any large files, I have
to rely on the kindness of others to get anything
at all.  The folks here let me use it, but won't even let me put it
on the network (FUD on their part, insurmountable so far)
It doesn't stop me from putting it on the network (I use another
ID), but it does limit my activities immensely.

