Problem: which SCSI cards are compatible with an old PC164 (not LX,SX)
board and the SRM console?

Answer: even after upgrading to the most recent SRM console, V5.6,
the choice is limited to cards with the following chips:
   53C810, 53C875, ISP1020, ISP1040, maybe also 53C895
53Cxxx chips were produced by different companies (NCR, Symbios)
and were used on many cards (see below for a non-comprehensive list),
ISPxxxx apparently only on Qlogic cards. A local alpha specialist
recommended 53Cxxx over ISPxxxx.

53C810 seems to support only Ultra narrow, the others UW, 53C895 also U2W.

With SRM 5.8, Adaptec cards should also work, but 5.8 is not available
for PC164.

Thanks,
   Gernot

Sources:
http://www.lsilogic.com/products/storage_standard_prod/hba/scsi/ultra_scsi/index.html
http://www.lsilogic.com/support/support+drivers/otheroem.html
http://www.qlogic.com/
http://www.qlogic.com/products/ultra_series/ultra_one_tech.asp
http://moon.hanya-n.org/comp/alpha/hct/scsi.html

List of SCSI cards (incomplete, with no guarantee that the SRM console
will boot):

53C875
======
ASUStek         SC-875
Centos Inc.     CI-4500U
Centos Inc.     CI-4500UW
Data Technology ULTRA-40
IOI Technology Corporation IOI-4204UW
J-Bond          JDC5075
JDR             MCT-PSCSI3-1
Koutech Systems, Inc. (Kouwell) KW-801V75
LSI logic       LSI8751D
LSI logic       LSI8751SPE
LSI logic       LSI8750SP
Promise Technology SCSIUltra40
Tekram          DC-390F

ISP 1020
========
Qlogic QLA1000-PI 

ISP 1040B, ISP 1040C
====================
Qlogic QLA1040
Qlogic QLA1041







