OK a little history info (and maybe a better question)...

In it's previous iteration I had the system as dual boot NT/RH5.1
I never could configure ARC properly to boot from the MILO on
the hard drive, but could get it to run MILO on the floppy.
>From there I would interactively boot linux.
The boot partition was sda8 and the boot command that
worked was:

MILO> boot:sda8:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda8

When trying to upgrade to RH 6.2, the additional packages I wanted to
add ran it out of disc space.  Every attempt to repartition the drive
would lock up the installation.  Since I don't use NT on the system anyway,
I went for a fresh install.  That worked.

Purely by luck I stumbled onto a new MILO boot command.  But it is
two stage:  

MILO> boot: sda1
boot: linux

The Milo.conf is 

image = /boot/vmlinuz-2.2.14-6.0
label = linux
root = /dev/sda1

I would like to do a single line boot again, but if I can't, it's OK

Ultimately, I would like it to autoboot, but it's a minor issue...

