On Thu, Jan 31, 2002 at 03:13:53PM +0100, Heid Oliver wrote:
>
> For a long time now, I want to replace the kernel QLogic driver by the one
> mentioned below, but it seems to be available only as a module. So is it
> possible at all to >boot< from the ISP controller with the new driver, for
> the module resides on HD and has to be loaded first? Or is it possible to
> boot with the old kernel driver, and then insmod the new driver module??
> Doesn't the boot device driver have to be compiled into the kernel?!

There are patches available on that site (www.feral.com) that
integrate the driver into a kernel source tree, including
configuration option(s). You are NOT forced to use a module, if you
don't want to. However, IIRC, you MUST NOT configure the old QLogic
driver in order to be asked if you want the NEW one.

I have successfully integrated the new driver into a RH kernel source
tree from 7.1, built a kernel with it in (not as a module), re-created
the ISO and successfully installed on a number of boxes that were
impossible to install the original on (AS500 and AS800, both of which
have QLogic 1020 on mobo and nearly always come with CD and HDD on
that single SCSI bus).

--Jay++

